From: Win4Wine contributors
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: anchor external taskbar grippers to their public header

Actual Japanese XP public rendering matches the theme-defined cross-axis
thickness at the band header origin with its full long axis. Let the local
theme margins and tiling supply the repeated grip pixels. Preserve native
band hit/drag geometry and opt-in boundaries. No Microsoft resources or code.

--- a/dlls/uxtheme/rebar.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/rebar.c
@@ -94,10 +94,11 @@
         /* Erase only the native gripper header; child/title/chevron rendering
          * and all native hit regions and dragging remain unchanged. */
         DrawThemeParentBackground(hwnd, dc, &header);
-        grip.left = header.left + (header.right - header.left - size.cx) / 2;
-        grip.top = header.top + (header.bottom - header.top - size.cy) / 2;
-        grip.right = grip.left + size.cx;
-        grip.bottom = grip.top + size.cy;
+        /* Native bands anchor the gripper at the header origin. The theme
+         * supplies its cross-axis thickness, spacing and long-axis tiling. */
+        grip = header;
+        if (vertical) grip.bottom = grip.top + size.cy;
+        else grip.right = grip.left + size.cx;
         DrawThemeBackground(theme, dc, part, 0, &grip, &header);
     }
 done:
